{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1547426-could-a-cainite-spend-blood-sleeping","id":1547426,"title":"Could a cainite spend blood sleeping?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-01-01T09:50:50-08:00","id":1547426,"title":"Could a cainite spend blood sleeping?","content":"First of all, Happy New Year!<br /> Now to the question, I mean, in the case of a particular vivid dream, if the cainite tried to use blood to boost his physical attributes in the dream, would he have spent those after waking up?<br /> What's your take on that?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-01T11:25:47-08:00","id":1547427,"title":"","content":"I would say yes<br /> I mean there is that flaw <br /> <br /> Nightmares (1pt. Flaw)<br /> You experience horrendous nightmares every time you sleep, and memories of them haunt you during your waking hours. Upon awakening, you must make a Willpower roll (difficulty 7) or lose a die on all actions for that night. A botched Willpower roll indicates that, even when awake, you still believe that you are locked in a nightmare.<br /> <br /> Simple little flaw, but very interresting suggesting vampires can dream and can have nightmares druing sleeping<br /> And in relation the question proves the nightmares/dreams effect could linger, in this case a dice loss or even not realizing the vampire is not dreaming - meaning the vampire dreams could be so vivid it is hard to distinguish them from reality<br /> So by following this logic if the vampire had a dream where he used his blood to be stronger... that blood is gone","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-01T12:01:38-08:00","id":1547429,"title":"","content":"I would allow blood to be spent due to a nightmare, but the act of burning the point would wake the vampire up.<br /> <br /> For dramatic effect a cainite might jerk awake to find their bedding torn and their Protean claws out, having spent the blood point due to a nightmare of fighting a foe. However, I wouldn't allow multiple blood points to be spent while dreaming because there are many abilities which manipulate dreams, usually at a safe distance, which means a foe could just force the target kindred to burn their entire blood pool in one days sleep and thus force them into torpor.<br /> <br /> It's not as straight forward as a mage making real sunlight suddenly appear, but it is almost as deadly because it completely takes the character out of commission for years or decades. The only thing that can save them is their friends waking them up early or their own security measures keeping them hidden or safe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-01T13:18:31-08:00","id":1547431,"title":"","content":"On a very baseline level, vampires are most certainly capable of spending blood in their sleep; the books provide examples of this.<br /> <br /> However, given that the Nightmare Flaw doesn't risk losing blood to dreams, I would generally not allow this scenario. It just feels like a way to cheese the system: Either it's giving STs fiat power to lower a character's blood pool because of a bad dream, or it's giving players a chance to activate a bunch of stuff right before waking up in the case of an unpleasant intrusion or the like. If a player really just wants their character to wake up hungrier... I'd allow it but you don't usually see many folks do that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-01T21:25:05-08:00","id":1547442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I would say yes<br /> I mean there is that flaw<br /> <br /> Nightmares (1pt. Flaw)<br /> You experience horrendous nightmares every time you sleep, and memories of them haunt you during your waking hours. Upon awakening, you must make a Willpower roll (difficulty 7) or lose a die on all actions for that night. A botched Willpower roll indicates that, even when awake, you still believe that you are locked in a nightmare. </div> </div> </div>Yes, I know this flaw and in like 90% of the groups I've storytelled in the last more than 200 years one of the PCs has it, I sincerely don't know why, but there's always one player who choses this flaw and to be honest, I like it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For dramatic effect a cainite might jerk awake to find their bedding torn and their Protean claws out, having spent the blood point due to a nightmare of fighting a foe. However, I wouldn't allow multiple blood points to be spent while dreaming because there are many abilities which manipulate dreams, usually at a safe distance, which means a foe could just force the target kindred to burn their entire blood pool in one days sleep and thus force them into torpor.<br /> \u200b </div> </div> </div>Yes, I'm aware of your worries, but I don't have such fears, such things are generally somewhat easily dealt with, but I see your worry here with potential rule's lawyers, if I notice any abuse in any rule in the game, I just disallow it and end of the story. In my early years as a Storyteller I was somewhat worried about people who want to abuse rules, nowadays it's as simple as saying &quot;no, you can't&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> However, given that the Nightmare Flaw doesn't risk losing blood to dreams, I would generally not allow this scenario. It just feels like a way to cheese the system: Either it's giving STs fiat power to lower a character's blood pool because of a bad dream, or it's giving players a chance to activate a bunch of stuff right before waking up in the case of an unpleasant intrusion or the like. If a player really just wants their character to wake up hungrier... I'd allow it but you don't usually see many folks do that. </div> </div> </div>Same as above, I just had this crazy (but not that original, I know) idea of making an entire session a nightmare only for the group to wake up later and realize it and then I'm thinking about how to pull this off and as I'm sure players are going to try to spend blood if they notice a &quot;combat situation&quot;, I'm anticipating and was kind of curious about other people's opinion on the matter. I like the idea of consulting other people's opinion, especially since Storytelling can feel kind of lonely sometimes and I do it since I was a child. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-02T00:31:41-08:00","id":1547446,"title":"","content":"So... the issue is that's sorta coming at the question backwards. If you asked, &quot;I'm going to run a scene where the PCs are secretly asleep, would you let them spend blood in the dream, and if so would they have to actually spend blood?&quot; I think you'd have gotten different responses.<br /> <br /> I would certainly let players spend &quot;dream&quot; blood for such a setup, but as noted not charge them for it when they wake up. We do all sorts of things in our dreams without actually doing them in reality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-02T09:52:43-08:00","id":1547459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1547426-could-a-cainite-spend-blood-sleeping?p=1547446#post1547446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So... the issue is that's sorta coming at the question backwards. If you asked, &quot;I'm going to run a scene where the PCs are secretly asleep, would you let them spend blood in the dream, and if so would they have to actually spend blood?&quot; I think you'd have gotten different responses.<br /> <br /> I would certainly let players spend &quot;dream&quot; blood for such a setup, but as noted not charge them for it when they wake up. We do all sorts of things in our dreams without actually doing them in reality.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, it would have been better if I asked the question differently, perhaps, but at the same time the results may vary. And also yes, I understand your point about not being able to spend &quot;real&quot; blood, but sometimes I think that for the sake of a story it can be interesting to blur the line between dreams and reality. I've been thinking a lot about these questions lately.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-04T04:47:49-08:00","id":1547512,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1547426-could-a-cainite-spend-blood-sleeping?p=1547459#post1547459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, it would have been better if I asked the question differently, perhaps, but at the same time the results may vary. And also yes, I understand your point about not being able to spend &quot;real&quot; blood, but sometimes I think that for the sake of a story it can be interesting to blur the line between dreams and reality. I've been thinking a lot about these questions lately.</div> </div> </div> </div>As always, do what works for your table. Like Heavy Arms, I'd allow them to spend &quot;dream blood&quot; but wouldn't deduct any actual blood points. Otherwise, it sucks for your players. <br /> <br /> On a related note: &quot;it was all a dream&quot; stories can be unsatisfying if they mean achievements get undermined or players feel &quot;cheated&quot;. One way around that is to make sure the dream conflicts have meaning in the real-world, too\u2014e.g., if they're being harassed by an ancient Ravnos in torpor, maybe defeating the dream allows them to locate his resting place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}